/* Additional source details and recall checks. Original source pages remain intact. */
(() => {
const byId=id=>window.LESSONS.find(x=>x.id===id);
byId('villi').text+=`<h3>Most water is absorbed in the small intestine<br>大部分水在小腸被吸收</h3><p>Absorption of digested food lowers the water potential in blood. Water follows by osmosis. The highly folded surface and many villi also support water absorption.<br>已消化食物被吸收後，血液水勢降低，水隨滲透作用被吸收；折疊的表面及大量絨毛有助水分吸收。</p><p class="refs">Source: 7.5–7.6, PDF p.4; concept-check answers p.20–21.</p>`;
byId('assimilation').text+=`<h3>Iron and haemoglobin · 鐵與血紅蛋白</h3><p>Iron from spinach is taken up by cells to make haemoglobin. This is assimilation. Spinach plants obtain food by photosynthesis (autotrophic nutrition).<br>菠菜中的鐵被細胞攝取以製造血紅蛋白，屬同化作用。菠菜植物以光合作用自製食物，屬自養營養。</p>`;
byId('liver').text+=`<h3>Application: liver cirrhosis<br>應用題：肝硬化</h3><p>The supplied concept check associates liver cirrhosis with reduced bile production and anaemia. It does not select increased production of hydrogen peroxide.<br>原概念題將肝硬化與膽汁製造減少及貧血聯繫；答案沒有選擇「過氧化氫製造增加」。</p><p class="refs">Source: 7.6–7.7, PDF p.15 Q5, with supplied answer B on p.17.</p>`;
byId('liver').text+=`<p class="refs">Optional molecular view: the carotene conversion sketch shows the retinal form of vitamin A, with hydrogen atoms and subsequent reactions abbreviated. Compound references: <a href="https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/beta-carotene" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PubChem β-carotene</a> and <a href="https://pubchem.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/compound/Retinal" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">PubChem retinal</a>.<br>分子細節選項以視黃醛形式示意維生素A，氫原子及後續反應已簡化；此化學細節不屬原筆記的考核要求。</p>`;
byId('applications').text+=`<h3>Dialysis-tubing model · 透析管模型</h3><table><tr><th>Model component 模型部分</th><th>Represents 代表</th></tr><tr><td>Dialysis tubing 透析管</td><td>Small intestine 小腸</td></tr><tr><td>Surrounding solution 外面的溶液</td><td>Blood 血液</td></tr><tr><td>Water bath at 37 °C<br>37 °C 水浴</td><td>Body temperature 體溫</td></tr></table><p>In the supplied validity question, rinse the dialysis tubing with distilled water before placing it in the test tubes, so material on the outside does not contaminate the surrounding solution.<br>原有效性題選擇先用蒸餾水沖洗透析管，再放入試管，避免外表的物質污染周圍溶液。</p><p class="refs">Source: 7.5–7.6, PDF p.3 and p.14 Q4–5; supplied answers p.20.</p>`;
byId('egestion').text+=`<h3>Complete large-intestine summary<br>大腸筆記完整要點</h3><table><thead><tr><th>Item 項目</th><th>Points from the notes 筆記要點</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Large intestine 大腸</td><td>No digestion in this course summary; most food has already been absorbed in the small intestine. Final absorption of water, minerals and vitamins. Colon compacts faeces; rectum temporarily stores faeces.<br>本課程總結列為沒有消化；大部分食物已在小腸吸收。最後吸收水、礦物質及維生素。結腸壓實糞便，直腸暫存糞便。</td></tr><tr><td>Faeces 糞便</td><td>Undigested and unabsorbed material: dietary fibre, bile pigments (brown), bacteria (smell), dead cells, mucus and a little water.<br>未消化及未吸收物質：膳食纖維、膽色素（棕色）、細菌（氣味）、死細胞、黏液及少量水。</td></tr><tr><td>Watery 水多</td><td>Diarrhoea linked to osmosis; or peristalsis too fast, leaving insufficient time to absorb water.<br>與滲透作用相關的腹瀉；或蠕動過快，沒有足夠時間吸水。</td></tr><tr><td>Oily 油多</td><td>The notes associate this with a pancreas / pancreatic-lipase problem.<br>筆記將此與胰臟／胰脂肪酶問題聯繫。</td></tr><tr><td>Blood 帶血</td><td>The notes link this with damage to the alimentary canal, and note that blood from further along the route is less bright red.<br>筆記將此與消化道受損聯繫，並提到較遠處的血較不鮮紅。</td></tr><tr><td>Constipation 便秘</td><td>Insufficient dietary fibre and water.<br>膳食纖維及水不足。</td></tr><tr><td>After partial large-intestine removal<br>切除部分大腸後的題目</td><td>Less water absorbed → more watery faeces. In the supplied postoperative question, a low-fibre diet slows peristalsis, allowing more time for water absorption.<br>吸水減少 → 糞便更稀。原題的術後情境中，低纖維飲食令蠕動減慢，增加吸水時間。</td></tr></tbody></table><h3>Sphincters · 括約肌</h3><table><tr><th>Name 名稱</th><th>Location 位置</th></tr><tr><td>Cardiac sphincter 賁門括約肌</td><td>Oesophagus–stomach junction 食道與胃交界</td></tr><tr><td>Pyloric sphincter 幽門括約肌</td><td>Stomach–duodenum junction 胃與十二指腸交界</td></tr><tr><td>Anal sphincter 肛門括約肌</td><td>Anus 肛門</td></tr></table><h3>Energy balance in the surgery question<br>手術題中的能量平衡</h3><p>Removing part of the small intestine reduces digestion / absorption and energy input. If input is less than output, stored reserves such as fat are broken down to supply energy.<br>切除部分小腸令消化／吸收及能量攝入減少；若攝入少於消耗，脂肪等儲備會被分解供能。</p><p class="refs">Source: 7.6–7.7, PDF p.18 and p.21–22. These are the supplied course and examination contexts.</p>`;
byId('applications').text+=`<h3>Microscopy & nutrient deficiency<br>顯微鏡與營養缺乏</h3><p>Damaged microvilli reduce surface area. Damaged carrier proteins can also reduce amino-acid absorption. Vitamin C deficiency causes scurvy; iron deficiency causes anaemia in the supplied case study.<br>微絨毛受損令表面積減少；載體蛋白受損亦可減少氨基酸吸收。原個案中，維生素 C 缺乏造成壞血病，鐵缺乏造成貧血。</p><p>For magnification, use image size ÷ actual size, with the same units. The original supplied example has a magnification of 62×. Keep biological drawings faithful to observable shape, with a title, cell membranes and nuclei labelled as required.<br>放大率＝圖像大小 ÷ 實際大小，先統一單位。原例答案為 62 倍。生物繪圖需符合可見形狀，並按題目要求加標題、細胞膜及細胞核標示。</p><h3>Experimental reasoning · 實驗推論</h3><p>In the supplied lipase question, pH stops changing when substrate is used up, or the enzyme becomes denatured under the stated conditions. A control without lipase tests whether lipase is needed for the pH change. The stated answer mentions pH 6.5 in that experiment.<br>原脂肪酶實驗中，底物耗盡或酶在該條件下變性可令 pH 停止改變；不含脂肪酶的對照可驗證 pH 改變是否需要脂肪酶。答案在該實驗中提及 pH 6.5。</p><p>A blocked pancreatic duct prevents pancreatic juice reaching the duodenum: fat in faeces increases and protein digestion becomes less effective. In the supplied MCQ, bile can still help neutralize chyme, so the answer does not select “chyme remains acidic”.<br>胰管阻塞令胰液不能到達十二指腸：糞便脂肪增加，蛋白質消化效率降低。原選擇題中，膽汁仍可協助中和食糜，因此答案不選「食糜維持酸性」。</p><h3>Absorption sites in the summary figures<br>總結圖中的吸收位置</h3><p>The supplied diagrams show water and alcohol absorption in the stomach (very little monosaccharide), extensive nutrient absorption in the small intestine, and final water, mineral and vitamin absorption in the large intestine. See original diagrams for the course's specific transport labels.<br>原圖列出胃吸收水及酒精（少量單糖）、小腸廣泛吸收營養素、大腸最後吸收水、礦物質及維生素。各物質的課程運輸標示請對照原圖。</p>`;
const additions={
villi:[
 ['Which feature shortens diffusion distance? 哪項縮短擴散距離？',['Many mitochondria 大量線粒體','One-cell-thick epithelium 單層上皮','A long intestine 很長的小腸'],1,'A thin, one-cell-thick lining shortens the distance across the epithelium. 單層上皮縮短穿過上皮的距離。'],
 ['Why do capillaries carry absorbed molecules away quickly? 微血管迅速帶走分子有何作用？',['Maintains a steep concentration gradient 維持陡濃度梯度','Makes food molecules larger 使食物分子增大','Stops osmosis 阻止滲透'],0,'Rapid removal keeps the concentration gradient steep, increasing diffusion rate. 迅速移走分子可維持陡濃度梯度，加快擴散。'],
 ['What powers active transport? 主動運輸依靠甚麼？',['Energy from respiration 呼吸作用的能量','Bile pigment 膽色素','Dietary fibre 膳食纖維'],0,'Mitochondria carry out aerobic respiration and supply ATP for active transport. 線粒體進行有氧呼吸，供應 ATP。']
],
transport:[
 ['Which vitamins enter lacteals in the notes? 哪些維生素進入乳糜管？',['B and C','A, D, E and K','Only C'],1,'Fat-soluble vitamins A, D, E and K follow the lipid route. 脂溶性維生素 A、D、E、K 隨脂質途徑運輸。'],
 ['Where do fatty acids and glycerol recombine? 脂肪酸和甘油在哪裏重組？',['In epithelial cells of villi 在絨毛上皮細胞內','In the heart 在心臟','In the colon 在結腸'],0,'The supplied notes place recombination into triglycerides in epithelial cells. 筆記指出甘油三酯在上皮細胞內重組。'],
 ['Which vessel leaves the liver for the vena cava? 哪條血管由肝通向腔靜脈？',['Hepatic artery 肝動脈','Hepatic portal vein 肝門靜脈','Hepatic vein 肝靜脈'],2,'The hepatic vein carries processed blood away from the liver. 肝靜脈將經肝處理的血液帶走。']
],
assimilation:[
 ['Which is assimilation? 哪項屬同化？',['Glucose enters a villus capillary 葡萄糖進入絨毛微血管','A cell uses iron to make haemoglobin 細胞利用鐵製造血紅蛋白','Fibre leaves through the anus 纖維經肛門排出'],1,'Cell uptake and use of absorbed nutrients is assimilation. 細胞攝取及利用已吸收營養素屬同化。'],
 ['Where is excess glucose stored as glycogen? 過量葡萄糖可在哪裏轉成糖原儲存？',['Liver and muscles 肝及肌肉','Only in lacteals 只在乳糜管','In the gall bladder 膽囊'],0,'The supplied notes list the liver and muscles as glycogen stores. 筆記列出肝及肌肉儲存糖原。'],
 ['Which is a use of lipids? 哪項是脂質的用途？',['Make cell membranes 製造細胞膜','Make dietary fibre 製造膳食纖維','Form urea directly 直接形成尿素'],0,'Lipids are used for energy storage, cell membranes and sex hormones. 脂質用於儲能、細胞膜及性激素。']
],
glucose:[
 ['After a sugary drink, liver glycogen… 飲用含糖飲品後，肝糖原會：',['Decrease 減少','Increase 增加','Leave in bile 隨膽汁離開'],1,'Raised blood glucose increases insulin and glucose conversion to glycogen. 血糖升高令胰島素增加，促進葡萄糖轉成糖原。'],
 ['After a high-protein meal, more urea leaves via… 高蛋白飲食後，較多尿素經哪裏離開肝？',['Hepatic vein 肝靜脈','Hepatic artery 肝動脈','Lacteal 乳糜管'],0,'The liver forms urea by deamination; it leaves in the hepatic vein. 肝脫氨形成尿素，經肝靜脈離開。'],
 ['Which hormone increases when blood glucose is low? 血糖低時哪種激素增加？',['Insulin 胰島素','Glucagon 升糖素','Bile 膽汁'],1,'Glucagon increases, promoting breakdown of liver glycogen to glucose. 升糖素增加，促進肝糖原分解成葡萄糖。']
],
liver:[
 ['Which is stored in the liver? 哪項儲存於肝？',['Iron and fat-soluble vitamins 鐵及脂溶性維生素','Undigested fibre 未消化纖維','Pancreatic juice 胰液'],0,'The liver stores glycogen, iron and vitamins A, D, E and K. 肝儲存糖原、鐵及維生素 A、D、E、K。'],
 ['Why is insulin ineffective orally? 為何口服胰島素無效？',['It is digested as a protein 它是蛋白質，會被消化','It is dietary fibre 它是膳食纖維','The liver turns it into bile 肝將它轉成膽汁'],0,'Digestive enzymes break down protein insulin before it can function intact. 消化酶將蛋白質胰島素分解，使其不能完整發揮作用。'],
 ['Bile enters which organ through the bile duct? 膽汁經膽管進入哪裏？',['Rectum 直腸','Duodenum 十二指腸','Heart 心臟'],1,'Bile enters the duodenum and helps emulsify fat and neutralize acidic chyme. 膽汁進入十二指腸，協助乳化脂肪及中和酸性食糜。']
],
egestion:[
 ['Which normally occurs in healthy faeces? 健康糞便通常含有甚麼？',['Red blood cells and no water 紅血球而沒有水','Bacteria and water 細菌及水','Only glucose 只有葡萄糖'],1,'The supplied answer selects bacteria and water; faeces also contain other unabsorbed residues. 答案選細菌及水，糞便亦有其他未吸收殘餘物。'],
 ['Why can fast peristalsis cause watery faeces? 為何蠕動過快可令糞便較稀？',['Less time for water absorption 吸水時間較少','More glycogen is made 製造更多糖原','More iron is stored 儲存更多鐵'],0,'Less time in the intestine means less water absorption and more water remaining in faeces. 腸內停留時間減少，吸水較少，糞便留下更多水。'],
 ['Where are faeces temporarily stored? 糞便暫存在哪裏？',['Liver 肝','Rectum 直腸','Duodenum 十二指腸'],1,'The rectum temporarily stores faeces before egestion. 直腸在排遺前暫存糞便。']
],
applications:[
 ['Why may lactose intolerance cause diarrhoea? 乳糖不耐症為何可導致腹瀉？',['Undigested lactose lowers lumen water potential 未消化乳糖令腸腔水勢下降','Lactose turns into fibre 乳糖變成纖維','Lactase increases water absorption 乳糖酶增加吸水'],0,'Insufficient lactase leaves lactose unabsorbed; water absorption is reduced. 乳糖酶不足令乳糖未被消化及吸收，減少水分吸收。'],
 ['What causes the pH fall in a lipase experiment? 脂肪酶實驗中甚麼令 pH 下降？',['Fatty acid production 產生脂肪酸','Glycogen production 產生糖原','Oxygen production 產生氧'],0,'Lipase releases fatty acids from lipids, lowering pH. 脂肪酶將脂質分解，釋出脂肪酸，令 pH 下降。'],
 ['Why omit lipase from a control tube? 為何對照試管不加脂肪酶？',['Test whether lipase is needed for pH change 驗證 pH 改變是否需要脂肪酶','Make bile salts 製造膽鹽','Cause deamination 引起脫氨'],0,'The control isolates the role of lipase in the pH change. 對照可顯示脂肪酶對 pH 改變的作用。']
]};
Object.entries(additions).forEach(([id,questions])=>questions.forEach(([q,options,answer,explain])=>byId(id).questions.push({q,options,answer,explain})));
})();
